1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,260
Hey! Let's start with the single biggest problem on Exam 2: a

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:09,549
form plus JavaScript validation. It's worth anywhere from 46 to 78 points,

3
00:00:09,649 --> 00:00:13,124
so if you only master one thing, make it this one.

4
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,828
First, the HTML. The form tag's action says where the data goes,

5
00:00:19,928 --> 00:00:24,556
here process dot PHP, and method equals post says how it's sent.

6
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:27,911
Each input gets two attributes that look alike but do

7
00:00:28,011 --> 00:00:31,462
different jobs. The name is the key the server receives.

8
00:00:31,562 --> 00:00:35,014
The id is what your JavaScript uses with getElementById.

9
00:00:35,083 --> 00:00:38,406
And value gives the field its starting text, so

10
00:00:38,506 --> 00:00:41,247
the route box already says M D dash 95.

11
00:00:41,316 --> 00:00:44,052
Now the buttons. A plain button tag with no

12
00:00:44,152 --> 00:00:47,152
type is a submit button by default. Type equals

13
00:00:47,252 --> 00:00:50,384
reset clears the form back to its default values.

14
00:00:50,483 --> 00:00:54,703
Finally, the script hooks our validation function to the submit event.

15
00:00:55,083 --> 00:00:58,820
Exam trap. A button with no type attribute submits the form.

16
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:02,145
If you want it to clear, write type equals reset. If

17
00:01:02,245 --> 00:01:05,471
you want it to do neither, write type equals button.

18
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:11,551
Look closely at this line. We assign the function

19
00:01:11,651 --> 00:01:15,223
itself to window dot onsubmit. No parentheses. The browser

20
00:01:15,323 --> 00:01:17,882
will call it for us when the user submits.

21
00:01:17,950 --> 00:01:21,660
Inside, the return value is the whole game. Return false,

22
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:25,338
and the submission is blocked. The page just stays put.

23
00:01:25,416 --> 00:01:28,988
Return true, and the form is sent to the action URL.

24
00:01:29,383 --> 00:01:33,714
Exam trap. If you write validateRequest with parentheses, the function

25
00:01:33,814 --> 00:01:37,196
runs once, right when the page loads, and onsubmit gets

26
00:01:37,296 --> 00:01:40,995
its return value instead of the function. That costs points.

27
00:01:44,083 --> 00:01:49,150
Here's a problem written the way the exam writes them. Read the requirements

28
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:54,046
carefully, because every bullet is a check you'll be graded on. One: the

29
00:01:54,146 --> 00:01:58,193
name can't be blank, and a name made of only spaces counts as

30
00:01:58,293 --> 00:02:02,205
blank. Two: the route is a state, a dash, and a number. The

31
00:02:02,305 --> 00:02:05,944
state must be M D or V A in any capitalization, and the

32
00:02:06,044 --> 00:02:10,432
number must be between 1 and 999. Three: show one alert that lists

33
00:02:10,532 --> 00:02:15,463
every error, not one alert per error. And four: if everything's valid, ask

34
00:02:15,563 --> 00:02:18,999
the user to confirm, and only send if they click OK.

35
00:02:22,083 --> 00:02:25,863
Step one. We start with an empty error string. The plan is to

36
00:02:25,963 --> 00:02:29,807
collect every problem in here, and only alert once at the end.

37
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:33,670
Then we read the name field's value. Remember, dot value

38
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:37,264
is always a string, even when the user typed digits.

39
00:02:37,333 --> 00:02:41,832
We trim it, which removes spaces from both ends, and compare it to

40
00:02:41,932 --> 00:02:45,873
the empty string. If it's blank, we tack on, bar, No name.

41
00:02:46,266 --> 00:02:50,174
Exam trap. Comparing the name to an empty string without

42
00:02:50,274 --> 00:02:54,110
trim misses an input of just spaces. Always trim first.

43
00:02:57,200 --> 00:03:00,546
Step two, the route. Split on the dash turns M

44
00:03:00,646 --> 00:03:03,767
D dash 95 into an array of two strings, and

45
00:03:03,867 --> 00:03:08,188
array destructuring drops them straight into state and num.

46
00:03:08,275 --> 00:03:13,104
We trim the state and lowercase it. That way capital M D, lowercase

47
00:03:13,204 --> 00:03:17,151
m d, and mixed case all compare equal to lowercase m d.

48
00:03:17,241 --> 00:03:22,773
If it's neither m d nor v a, add, Invalid state. Notice it's AND here:

49
00:03:22,873 --> 00:03:27,197
the state is bad only if it's not m d and also not v a.

50
00:03:27,275 --> 00:03:31,732
For the number, convert with Number. Then check isNaN first, and

51
00:03:31,832 --> 00:03:35,791
then the range. If any of those fail, add, Invalid route.

52
00:03:36,175 --> 00:03:40,124
A few Number facts worth memorizing. Number of an empty string

53
00:03:40,224 --> 00:03:44,174
is zero, which the less than one check catches. Number ignores

54
00:03:44,274 --> 00:03:47,898
surrounding spaces. And if the user typed no dash at all,

55
00:03:47,998 --> 00:03:51,099
num is undefined, and Number of undefined is NaN.

56
00:03:54,175 --> 00:03:57,525
Step three. If the error string isn't empty, show it

57
00:03:57,625 --> 00:04:00,843
in one alert and return false, so nothing is sent.

58
00:04:00,941 --> 00:04:06,109
Otherwise, build the confirmation message and return whatever window dot confirm

59
00:04:06,209 --> 00:04:10,125
returns. Confirm gives true when the user clicks OK and false

60
00:04:10,225 --> 00:04:13,681
for Cancel, which is exactly the value onsubmit needs.

61
00:04:14,075 --> 00:04:17,285
Exam trap. You have to return the result of confirm. If

62
00:04:17,385 --> 00:04:21,800
you just call confirm without returning it, the function returns undefined,

63
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:25,111
and the form gets sent even if the user clicked Cancel.

64
00:04:28,208 --> 00:04:31,896
Let's run it. The user typed only spaces for the name,

65
00:04:31,996 --> 00:04:35,404
and N Y dash 95 for the route, then clicks Submit.

66
00:04:35,475 --> 00:04:40,264
Trimming the name gives an empty string, so we add No name. The

67
00:04:40,364 --> 00:04:43,601
state is n y, which isn't m d or v a, so we

68
00:04:43,701 --> 00:04:48,335
add Invalid state. And 95 is in range, so the number is fine.

69
00:04:48,408 --> 00:04:51,488
So the user sees one alert with both errors, and

70
00:04:51,588 --> 00:04:54,404
since we return false, the form is not sent.

71
00:04:57,475 --> 00:05:00,422
Now a good one: Ann, and Md dash 95 with some

72
00:05:00,522 --> 00:05:04,485
extra spaces. The trim and the lowercase take care of those,

73
00:05:04,585 --> 00:05:08,007
so there are no errors, and the confirm box pops up.

74
00:05:08,075 --> 00:05:13,075
Click OK, confirm returns true, and the form is posted to process dot

75
00:05:13,175 --> 00:05:18,103
PHP. Click Cancel, it returns false, and the user stays on the page.

76
00:05:21,175 --> 00:05:25,888
Practice question 1. A field with id room holds a building and a

77
00:05:25,988 --> 00:05:30,326
room separated by a comma, like A V W comma 1112. Write the

78
00:05:30,426 --> 00:05:35,064
two checks: the building can't be blank, and the room must be a

79
00:05:35,164 --> 00:05:39,051
number from 1000 to 4999. Pause the video and try it.

80
00:05:47,341 --> 00:05:52,386
Same pattern as before, just splitting on a comma. Destructure into building and

81
00:05:52,486 --> 00:05:57,273
room. If the building is blank after trimming, add No building. Then convert

82
00:05:57,373 --> 00:06:01,003
the room with Number, and if it's NaN or out of range, add

83
00:06:01,103 --> 00:06:04,861
Invalid room. Notice that if the user types only I R B, room

84
00:06:04,961 --> 00:06:09,105
is undefined, Number makes it NaN, and the check still catches it.

85
00:06:13,175 --> 00:06:17,174
Practice question 2. The user forgets the dash and types M D

86
00:06:17,274 --> 00:06:21,889
95, with a valid name. Using our validateRequest, what does the alert

87
00:06:21,989 --> 00:06:25,579
say, and is the form sent? Pause the video and try it.

88
00:06:33,875 --> 00:06:38,803
Splitting on a dash that isn't there gives a one-element array. So state

89
00:06:38,903 --> 00:06:42,924
is the whole string, m d 95, which is an invalid state. And

90
00:06:43,024 --> 00:06:47,743
num is undefined, so Number gives NaN, which is an invalid route. The

91
00:06:47,843 --> 00:06:52,423
alert shows both errors, we return false, and the form is not sent.

92
00:06:56,508 --> 00:07:00,290
To recap. Hook it up with window dot onsubmit equals the

93
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:05,489
function, no parentheses. Read each value, then split, trim, lowercase, and

94
00:07:05,589 --> 00:07:09,648
convert with Number. Check isNaN and the range, and add each

95
00:07:09,748 --> 00:07:13,738
problem to one error string. If there are errors, one alert

96
00:07:13,838 --> 00:07:18,590
and return false. Otherwise, return window dot confirm. Nail this, and

97
00:07:18,690 --> 00:07:21,848
you've locked in the biggest chunk of the exam.

